       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline, which is 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and seizures. Nothing you've told me about the patient (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify going above the maximum.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **A usual dose:** The typical start is 25\u201350 mg once daily. It can be titrated in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least a week, up to 200 mg/day. I can enter any dose in that range.\n- **200 mg once daily:** This is the maximum dose.\n- **400 mg on purpose:** If this is a deliberate off-label dose, for example on a psychiatry recommendation, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the indication and who approved it. I'd also suggest checking an ECG and the patient's other serotonergic or QT-prolonging medications first.\n\nLet me know which you want and I'll enter it."
      }
